{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tidy drawing of the tree: Reingold and Tilford’s layered tree drawing as Walker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refined it, in Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert’s linear-time form."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree\/reingoldtilfordlayout()"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree\/reingoldTilfordLayout()"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV12GraphDrawingE21reingoldTilfordLayoutAD0E0VyxGyF","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"Trees","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"modules":[{"relatedModules":["Trees"],"name":"GraphDrawing"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift#L36","fileName":"ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift"},"title":"reingoldTilfordLayout()"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The root is at (0, 0) and a vertex at depth d has y = d. Children are placed left to right","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, vertices at one depth at least 1 apart along each subtree’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contour, and every parent centred over its first and last child. Where two subtrees are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pushed apart, the smaller subtrees between them are spaced evenly. A mirrored tree draws as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the reflection of the drawing, and isomorphic subtrees are drawn identically up to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"translation. Separations and centring give multiples of a power of ½, which are exact in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The even spacing divides a shift by the number of gaps, so values such as ±5\/6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"occur and are rounded, and a mirrored tree’s drawing then matches the reflection only to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rounding.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reingold and Tilford, “Tidier drawings of trees”, IEEE Transactions on Software"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Engineering SE-7(2), 1981."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Walker, “A node-positioning algorithm for general trees”, Software: Practice and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Experience 20(7), 1990."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert, “Improving Walker’s algorithm to run in linear time”,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Graph Drawing (GD 2002), LNCS 2528, 2002.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n) time and memory, with no recursion."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees","title":"Trees","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Drawing":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/drawing","abstract":[{"text":"A position in the plane for each vertex, in a fixed vertex order: what every layout in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module returns, and what a caller passes as a starting drawing.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}],"title":"Drawing"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing","type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","title":"GraphDrawing"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees/RootedTree/reingoldTilfordLayout()":{"kind":"symbol","conformance":